<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB1-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB1-002" ;
  triage:title "Ruling 1's retained seven-kind early-return path silently drops delivery_task/delivery_task_ack rows" ;
  triage:description "fenix critical design review, PR #1438 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1438#issuecomment-5648340494 (2026-09-12T20:01:44Z), reviewed at b06b3e262. crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/template_override_migration.rs:163 (if !has_template_kind_check(..) || table_sql...contains(\"'queue'\") { return Ok(()); }) inside the retained migrate_template_override_kinds_to_seven (:155), still called from shared_db.rs:763 before remove_template_override_kind_check (:248). End state is correct (verified by ensure_schema_removes_seven_kind_check_without_changing_stale_rows), but a pre-seven DB is rebuilt twice, the code carries two create-table + two copy paths, and copy_seven_kind_override_rows (:106-129) still silently drops delivery_task/delivery_task_ack rows -- design section 4.2 requires \"reported ... never silently re-mapped\"." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "design-debt" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "fenix critical review" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
